    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Anne of Green Gables–The Musical™ (Sensory Friendly Performance)"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Running Time: Act One 1h 10 | 20 Min Intermission | Act Two 50 Min As part of our efforts to be more accessible, the Centre is offering this Sensory Friendly Performance – designed to make theatre spaces more welcoming for audience members who may experience anxiety, are sensory-sensitive, or are not comfortable with the conventions of a theatre setting. — See Prince Edward Island’s iconic redhead on stage this summer! This Canadian classic is a humorous, touching, and dynamic musical that will inspire your imagination, tickle your funny bone, and mesmerize you with its graceful and exhilarating singing and dancing. This cherished family musical tells the poignant and funny story of a freckle-faced, red-haired orphan named Anne Shirley who arrives at the Bright River Railway Station full of hope for a new life. Her destination is the home of brother and sister Matthew and Marilla Cuthbert in Avonlea, Prince Edward Island. When she arrives at Green Gables, Anne is devastated when she discovers that the elderly siblings were expecting a boy from the orphanage, and then ecstatic when they decide to keep her. With her fiery temper, love of melodrama and romance, and penchant for misadventure, she brings laughter, [&hellip;]"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/keywords": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Dance, Music, On Stage, Theatre"
      }
    ],
