    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Inclusive Dance 6-Week Class"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Inclusive Dance in Charlottetown offers a safe, supportive, and welcoming dance class for students of all abilities. Inspired by the Boston Ballet’s renowned Adaptive Dance Program, this class is designed to break down barriers and make dance fully accessible to individuals with disabilities. Students explore movement, rhythm, and creative expression in a positive environment where their abilities are celebrated. Through guided activities and adaptive movement patterns, dancers gain confidence, develop motor skills, and experience the joy of dance in their own unique way.This Inclusive Dance program highlights each student’s strengths while encouraging creativity, connection, and self-expression—making it one of Charlottetown’s leading accessible dance classes for children, teens, and adults with diverse needs. Dates: Saturdays | January 24, January 31, February 7, February 14, February 21, February 28 Instructor: As a former dance umbrella student, Kayla Shaw-Mills is thrilled to to continue working with the dance umbrella program, as well as furthering other education initiatives. She has continued her dance training with George Brown College, Martha Graham School of Contemporary Dance, Boston Ballet’s Adaptive Dance Training, and has a BFA in Dance Education at York University. Kayla is excited to be teaching My Parent and Me, Creative Movement, Inclusive Dance, and contemporary [&hellip;]"
      }
    ],
