        "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/fr/event/6-week-series-teen-improv/%23tickets"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "fr",
        "@value": "Teen Improv 6-Week Class"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "fr",
        "@value": "Level up your social skills, confidence, and creativity in this high-energy teen improv class! Designed for beginners and returning performers, this program teaches quick-thinking games, instant scene creation, character building, and collaborative storytelling. With improv, there are no mistakes—only fun. Teens bring their energy, and together we create big laughs, build self-esteem, and spark imagination. It’s one of the best after-school activities in Charlottetown for teenagers who want to make friends, try something new, and discover just how funny and creative they can be. Perfect for ages 13–16 looking for engaging youth activities, performing arts programs. Fridays | January 16, January 23, January 30, February 6th, February 13, February 20. Register by clicking &#8220;Buy Tickets&#8221; Instructor: Cameron MacDonald has been performing on PEI from a young age. He has been trained in theatre by many over the years, from UPEI to the Confederation Centre of the Arts, but he attributes most of what he&#8217;s learned to his father of Annekenstein fame. He has been a member of Popalopalots improv for over a decade, and also leads the Heritage Players program."
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/keywords": [
      {
        "@language": "fr",
        "@value": "6 week series, Arts Education, Workshops"
      }
    ],
