        "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/fr/event/open-ballet/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "fr",
        "@value": "Open Ballet Course"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "fr",
        "@value": "Join us on Saturdays for an open ballet class designed for dancers who want to strengthen their technique and deepen their artistry. This traditionally structured ballet class is ideal for students looking to refine their skills, reinforce weekly training, and build a strong classical foundation. Dancers will work through a full barre and center, focusing on clean classical alignment, precision, musicality, balance, and strength. With supportive instruction in a professional studio environment, this class offers an excellent opportunity to grow, challenge yourself, and elevate your ballet technique. Perfect for dancers in Charlottetown seeking quality ballet training, weekend dance classes, or ongoing technique development. Saturdays | January 10, January 17, January 24, January 31, February 7, February 14 Instructor: Dominic Who has danced internationally with companies including Canada’s Ballet Jorgen, Les Grands Ballets, Ballet Theatre UK, Alberta Ballet, Chateau Versailles Spectacles, and currently with Opera Atelier and his own works. A graduate of the School of Alberta Ballet, he has toured multiple countries and performed in theatres including the Ed Mirvish Theatre and the Royal Opera House in Versailles. Having danced an extensive number of roles, including Albrecht from Giselle, Slave in Corsair, and Siegfried in Swan Lake, Dominic is now turning [&hellip;]"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/keywords": [
      {
        "@language": "fr",
