  {
    "@id": "_:g7856940",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Person"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/BerkleySilvermanHeadshot.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "fr",
        "@value": "Berkley Silverman"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "fr",
        "@value": "Berkley is absolutely thrilled to be making her Charlottetown Festival debut as Anne in Anne of Green Gables! She is deeply honoured to get to bring one of the most iconic Canadian stories to life. Credits include: the Canadian Premiere of Ride:The Musical (WJT), Bring it On! (Globe Theatre),  Girl Scout/Lydia cover in Beetlejuice (NCL), Olive in The 25th Annual Putnam County Spelling Bee (Shifting Ground Collective), Fiddler on the Roof, Evita, Shrek, The Prom (Drayton Entertainment), Blocked (TheaterWorks USA), Drama 101 (Toronto Fringe), Innocence Lost (Soulpepper), The Hockey Sweater (Segal Centre). Selected Film/TV/Voice: Reverse 1999 (OneLine Studios); Murdoch Mysteries (CBC/UKTV); Abducted on Prom Night (Lifetime); Workin Moms’ (Netflix), Cross (Amazon Prime). Berkley is best known for voicing Everest in Paw Patrol on Nickelodeon. Huge thanks to Ros, Steven, my NY team, TDZ, AMI, and my family and friends. I wouldn’t be here without all of you.  Biggest love goes to my incredible mom, who makes all of this possible. @berkleysilverman "
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "_:g7856960",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Person"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/JoemaFrith.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "fr",
        "@value": "Joema Firth"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "fr",
        "@value": "Joema Firth Charlottetown: Debut  Other Theatre: Disney's The Lion King (Mirvish), Mary Poppins, Little Mermaid (Rainbow Stage), Beautiful: The Carole King Musical (Drayton Ent.), Shrek: The Musical (YPT). I am so excited to be joining the great legacy that is Anne of Green Gables and can't wait to bring this show to you. Thank you so much to my friends and family for all the love and the team at Talent House for their constant support! "
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "_:g7856980",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Person"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://confederationcentre.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/HaKeenaManeso-1.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "fr",
        "@value": "Ha’Keena Maneso"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "fr",
        "@value": "Ha’Keena Maneso is a dancer, singer and actor originally from Moose Jaw, Saskatchewan. She is thrilled to be returning to Anne of Green Gables for her second year! Ha’Keena studied Musical Theatre at St. Lawrence College in Brockville, ON. Some of her previous credits include: Globe Theatre - Bring It On! (Nautica), Drayton Entertainment - Shrek The Musical (Gingy), Beautiful: A Carole King Musical (Shirelle), Ovation Theatre - Into The Woods (Little Red), Charlottetown Theatre Festival - Anne of Green Gables (Tillie Boulter), Jersey Boys, YES Theatre - Groundhog Day The Musical, Theatre Aquarius - Pollyanna (Fannie), A Christmas Story, Tweed and Company - Joseph and The Amazing Technicolour Dreamcoat (Brother), Stephenville Theatre Festival - 9 to 5 (Kathy), St. Lawrence College - Rocky Horror Picture Show (Magenta), Pippin (Leading Player), Apothecary (Lady), Cats (Bombalurina). Ha’Keena wants to thank her Kindred Spirits back home, her friends and family, for their love and support; she would not be here without you! "
      }
    ]
  },
